variable.notes:
The BloomReach Basket Object contains detailed conversion parameters for each product that was purchased. An example basket object that this variable might return:

{
   "items": [
        {
          "prod_id" : "pid123456",
          "sku": "sku789",.
          "name": "Cashmere Sweater",
          "quantity": "1",
          "price": "65.95"
        }
 }

## Detailed Basket Spec

Type: Object

This object contains a property called `items` which is an array of the product objects purchased. For each product in the `items` array, the following properties should be included as specified:

name: prod_id
type: String
example: "pid123456"
description: Product ID. Needs to match Product ID sent in feed.

name: sku
type: String
example: "sku789"
description: Product SKU. Should match SKU ID sent in feed. Only applies if you have SKUs.

name: name
type: String
example: "Cashmere Sweater"
description: Product Name.

name: quantity
type: Integer
example: 2
description: Quantity of this product in the basket

name: price
type: String
example: "pid123456"
description: Unit price *per* product, not the total price. If item is on sale, this is the unit sale price.

## Additional Examples

2 products, first product has a sku, second product does not have a sku:

{
   "items": [
        {
          "prod_id" : "pid123456",
          "sku": "sku789",.
          "name": "Cashmere Sweater",
          "quantity": "1",
          "price": "65.95"
        },
        {
          "prod_id" : "pid56789",
          "sku": "",
          "name": "Blue Skinny Jeans",
          "quantity": "2",
          "price": "79.99"
        }
      ]
 };

2 products, first product is a Product Bundle, second product is an individual product:

{
   "items": [
        {
          "prod_id" : "bundle223344",
          "sku": "",.
          "name": "Linen Bed Sheet Set",
          "quantity": "1",
          "price": "265.95"
        },
        {
          "prod_id" : "pid56789",
          "sku": "",
          "name": "Blue Skinny Jeans",
          "quantity": "2",
          "price": "79.99"
        }
      ]
};

## Additional Details 

If the item in the basket is a Product Collection, Product Bundle or Sku Set:
         (a)  Your Collection Pages have their own unique ID and are sold exactly like standalone products, then enter the collection ID in the prod_id 
                field. Make sure that this collection ID is sent in the feed in the product ID field.

         (b) Your Product Collections have their own unique ID, but cannot be purchased as a whole; only the collections' individual parts/products 
               can be purchased and each of these individual parts have their own ID. In this case, list all individual products in the basket and the 
               prod_id is the the ID of each product. Make sure that each product ID is sent in the feed in the product ID field.

         (c) Products that are a part of a Collection but can only be purchased from their own individual product page. In this case follow the same 
               guideline as described in (b)

## Custom Javascript Variable Example

This variable will normally be setup as the Custom JavaScript type. Here is an example of the function you might write. The example assumes you've implemented Google Enhanced Ecommerce and the purchase object is available on the data layer.

function () {
    var products = google_tag_manager[{{Container ID}}].dataLayer.get("ecommerce.purchase.products");
    var item;
    var items = [];

    if (products && products.length > 0) {
        for (var i = 0; i < products.length; i++) {
            console.log(products[i]);
            item = {};
            item.prod_id = products[i].id;
            item.name = products[i].name;
            item.quantity = products[i].quantity;
            item.price = products[i].price;
            items.push(item);
        }
    }

    return {"items": items};
}

